Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government - RED National Situatio=
n Report No. 6
As at 0800, Saturday 17 January 2026

Handling: OFFICIAL. Not for onward distribution outside government and LRF pa=
rtners.

A. Storm Fenella
Status: Recovery phase
Lead: Cumbria Resilience Forum and Lancashire Resilience Forum
Key points:
  - Cockremouth School: open as rest centre (run by Cumberland Council)
  - the Northside bridge: closed to all traffic
  - A591 near Thirlmere: remains closed (flooding)
  - Fellside: EVACUATED (run by Fellside Care Ltd)

B. Penrith water contamination
Status: Major incident declared. Response phase.
Lead: Cumbria Local Resilience Forum
Key points:
  - the Castle Park water station: OPEN for collection (run by United Utiliti=
es Water)
  - Eamont Moor Water Treatment Works: taken out of supply (run by United Uti=
lities)
  - Penrith LC: OPEN for collection

C. Central government
RED duty officer in contact with the LRF secretariats. Next report at 0800 to=
morrow.

Regards,
Sian Pryce
Resilience Adviser, RED, Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government

